{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"9f96a334a4ce6f6b05b4c9a95746297fd4a222a2dbaa53a29282cabccbdb6599","digest":{"component_or_area":"MCP server grounding_info schema initialization","key_entities":["rebar.mcp_server.build_server()","mcp.server.fastmcp.server.Settings","FastMCP","IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning","Settings.model_rebuild()","pydantic_settings.sources.utils","lifespan"],"problem_keywords":["pydantic settings","forward reference","incomplete field definition","warning","lifespan annotation","model rebuild"],"propositions":["MCP v1 Settings is defined before FastMCP under postponed annotations, leaving lifespan as an unresolved ForwardRef","First FastMCP construction triggers IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning from pydantic-settings 2.15 when the warning is promoted to an error","Calling Settings.model_rebuild() at the MCP import boundary in build_server resolves the annotation and eliminates the warning","build_server() must invoke Settings.model_rebuild() before FastMCP HTTP or stdio construction to ensure complete metadata","The fix adds no dependency, preserves optional MCP imports, and does not suppress the warning or downgrade pydantic-settings"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787690587955109001,"uuid":"ad136a26-75b7-4090-ae05-b1c9f08cad8b"}